* 2026-10-26 2.3.1.2
  fix Data Domain: all three disk tables (diskPropState, diskPerfState,
  diskErrState) now share one DiskStateTC classifier, so a neutral
  "available" disk no longer warns in diskPerformance/diskReliability and
  "absent" (disk present but not communicating) is now reported as warning
* 2026-10-26 2.3.1.1
  fix Data Domain: hardware-health disk_subsystem now reports each disk's
  diskPropState instead of a bare "OK"; only a "failed" disk warns, while
  "unknown" (reserved/empty slot) and "system" (management) disks are
  benign and an unrecognised state is reported UNKNOWN
* 2026-10-15 2.3.1
  cache the classification result
* 2026-09-29 2.3
  add Data Domain VTL (virtual tape library) health check to hardware-health
  fix Data Domain: AlertSubsystem no longer clears the OK messages of sibling
  subsystems checked before it (hardware-health output was unstable between runs)
* 2026-09-29 2.2
  add filesystem-free mode for Dell Data Domain

